    "title": {
      "zh": "晶体管开关",
      "en": "Transistor Switches"
    }
  },
  "stage": "explain",
  "title": {
    "zh": "一个信号怎样替芽芽开灯？",
    "en": "How Can a Signal Turn On a Lamp?"
  },
  "brief": {
    "zh": "沿两条路径找一找。一条把信号送到晶体管，另一条把电流送过红灯。",
    "en": "Trace two paths. One carries a signal to the transistor. The other carries current through the red LED."
  },
  "concept": {
    "zh": "基极电平与灯支路",
    "en": "Base input and lamp circuit"
  },
  "hints": [],
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": {
        "zh": "信号也能操作开关",
        "en": "A signal can work a switch"
      },
      "body": {
        "zh": "这个 NPN 晶体管有三个端。基极 B 接收控制信号，集电极 C 接灯支路，发射极 E 接电源的共同参考点 GND。",
        "en": "This NPN transistor has three terminals. Its base B receives the control signal, its collector C connects to the lamp circuit, and its emitter E connects to the shared reference GND."
      }
    },
    {
      "title": {
        "zh": "先看输入，再看灯",
        "en": "Check the input, then the lamp"
      },
      "body": {
        "zh": "在这块板上，LOW 是接近 GND 的低电平，记作 0。HIGH 是高电平，记作 1。HIGH 经基极电阻送来小电流，让晶体管导通。灯支路的开关也合上时，电源才会让电流流过 LED。",
        "en": "On this board LOW is a low voltage near GND and represents 0. HIGH is a high voltage and represents 1. A HIGH signal supplies a small current through the base resistor and turns on the transistor. With the lamp switch closed too, current from the supply can flow through the LED."
      }
    }
  ],
  "question": {
    "prompt": {
      "zh": "输入保持 HIGH，灯支路的开关却断开了。红灯会怎样？",
      "en": "The input stays HIGH, but the lamp switch is open. What happens to the LED?"
    },
    "options": [
      {
        "zh": "亮。基极有信号就够了",
        "en": "On. A base signal is enough"
      },
      {
        "zh": "灭。灯所在的支路还有缺口",
        "en": "Off. There is a gap in the lamp circuit"
      },
      {
        "zh": "一半时间亮，一半时间灭",
        "en": "It flashes half the time"
      }
    ],
    "correct": 1,
    "feedback": {
      "zh": "信号已让晶体管导通，断开的开关仍会阻断经过灯的电流。",
      "en": "The transistor is on, but the open switch still interrupts current through the lamp."
    }
  },
